\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Registration pipeline. The follow-up (moving) and baseline (fixed) PET/CT scans are aligned by an affine pre-registration, then by the LapIRN network, which predicts a dense deformation. Instance optimisation (IO) refines this deformation per pair before the moving scan is resampled into the fixed frame. Network training and IO use the same groups of loss terms: alignment, PET preservation, and deformation regularisation (Sec.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sect:objective}). \leavevmode {\color  {red}[TODO: Update the figure if the rigidity term or the IO-only variant should appear.]}}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{4}{Registration pipeline. The follow-up (moving) and baseline (fixed) PET/CT scans are aligned by an affine pre-registration, then by the LapIRN network, which predicts a dense deformation. Instance optimisation (IO) refines this deformation per pair before the moving scan is resampled into the fixed frame. Network training and IO use the same groups of loss terms: alignment, PET preservation, and deformation regularisation (Sec.~\ref {sect:objective}). \todo {Update the figure if the rigidity term or the IO-only variant should appear.}}{figure.1}{}}
